   $q$Why do the birds most likely repay "precisely what was marked" and then fly home?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They had very few twigs and little moss to spare.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The magpie treated her help as a debt, so they treated it as one too.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They wanted to punish the magpie for being proud.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstated-inference"},{"text":"They had forgotten how often the magpie helped them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The magpie treated her help as a debt, so they treated it as one too.$q$, $q$The magpie kept a record and called in her "debts," so the birds paid exactly what was owed and nothing more. They repay the full marked amount politely, which shows they remembered and were not trying to punish her.$q$, 'draft', '5022d12f-ce7f-5865-841f-2b29f7d165d3')
