   $q$Why does Bao most likely slide the board in front of Keisha at the end, and what does this show?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He forgot which slider controlled the house lights, which shows he was tired.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"He was afraid of making a final mistake, which shows he lacked confidence.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-evidence"},{"text":"Ms. Ferreira told him to return the board, which shows he follows directions.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He wants her to finish the show she has run for years, which shows respect for her.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He wants her to finish the show she has run for years, which shows respect for her.$q$, $q$Keisha "had run it for three years," and Bao gives her the last cue of opening night, a gesture of respect. He had memorized every cue and "hit every cue," so forgetting or fear does not fit, and Ms. Ferreira only says "Booth."$q$, 'draft', '35c073ad-d385-59ff-94db-6d992a259a4d')
