   $q$What can be inferred from the line "He says the measuring cup is in his wrists"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"His wrists ache from years of kneading.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"He lost the bakery's measuring cup.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"He has baked so often that he measures by feel.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He thinks measuring flour is a kind of cheating.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstated-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He has baked so often that he measures by feel.$q$, $q$The line follows "He never measures the flour anymore," so it means his hands know the right amount from long practice. The poem never says his wrists hurt or that measuring is wrong.$q$, 'draft', '38f58d7f-bce8-5256-98bf-e5eb274437e1')
